#!/bin/sh
# The USB mode chosen last, again after a boot: bridge while fpvos-usb's
# SAVED_MODE says so (a board without one always boots in normal mode).
# After the radio's client (S60) so bridge mode can take the chip from it.
case "${1:-}" in
	start)
		[ "$(/usr/sbin/fpvos-usb saved 2>/dev/null)" = bridge ] || exit 0
		echo "fpvos-usb: bridge mode, as saved"
		/usr/sbin/fpvos-usb mode bridge
		;;
	stop|restart|reload) ;;
	*) echo "Usage: $0 start" >&2; exit 1 ;;
esac
